    "settings": {},
    "subgraphDefs": {
      "ks_thin_film": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "color": "#f472b6",
            "id": "note_body",
            "position": {
              "x": 322,
              "y": 34
            },
            "size": {
              "h": 56,
              "w": 3602
            },
            "text": "**Thin film** — light reflected from the top and bottom of a film of thickness `d` interferes with path difference `2·n·d·cosθt`, where `cosθt = √(1 − (1 − N·V²)/n²)`.\nEach colour channel has a different wavelength, modelled as phase offsets (0, ⅓, ⅔) of `½ + ½ cos(2π(path·bands + offset))`. Not spectral — an art-directable approximation, cheap and portable."
          }
        ],
        "edges": {
